+# Staging verification runbook (Required item 1)
+
+Run these in order. Every script exits non-zero on failure and never prints secrets.
+
+## 0. Deploy
+Merge the branch, then redeploy BOTH Render services (customer and admin).
+VITE_* values are baked in at build time, so use a full redeploy, not a restart.
+
+## 1. Health  (blocker 1)
+    STAGING_CUSTOMER_URL=https://<customer>.onrender.com \
+    STAGING_ADMIN_URL=https://<admin>.onrender.com \
+    node scripts/staging/smoke.mjs
+
+Expected: `/api/health` returns 200 with `database: healthy` on both services.
+The probe reads the public `products` catalog as anon. It does not need, and must
+never be given, any access to `profiles`.
+
+If it still returns 503, the body names which check failed. A 42501 on `products`
+means migration 0031 (anon SELECT on the catalog) has not been applied to staging.
+
+## 2. Supabase Auth URLs  (blocker 2, manual)
+Supabase dashboard > Authentication > URL Configuration:
+- Site URL = customer URL
+- Redirect URLs = `https://<customer>.onrender.com/**` and `https://<admin>.onrender.com/**`
+Authentication > Sign In / Providers > Email: note whether "Confirm email" is on.
+
+## 3. Auth and admin separation  (blocker 2)
+Create two test users in Authentication > Users (a customer and an admin).
+Set the admin role in the SQL editor (not from the app), for example:
+
+    update auth.users set raw_app_meta_data = coalesce(raw_app_meta_data,'{}'::jsonb) || '{"role":"admin"}'::jsonb
+    where email = '<admin test email>';
+
+Then:
+
+    STAGING_SUPABASE_URL=... STAGING_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=... \
+    STAGING_CUSTOMER_EMAIL=... STAGING_CUSTOMER_PASSWORD=... \
+    STAGING_ADMIN_EMAIL=...    STAGING_ADMIN_PASSWORD=... \
+    node scripts/staging/auth-check.mjs --signup --try-escalation
+
+`smoke.mjs` already covers the UI side: the admin button exists only on the admin host,
+and a signed-out visitor gets the admin login, not the panel.
+Manual finish: in a browser, log in as the customer on the ADMIN site and confirm
+the admin panel stays closed; log in as the admin and confirm it opens.
+
+Admin URLs: the app is a single-page app with no /admin path. The admin host opens on
+the storefront view and the Admin button in the navbar switches to the admin view.
+
+## 4. Deployed bundle scan  (blocker 4)
+Export the same secret values you set on Render into your LOCAL shell (they are compared
+in memory only), then:
+
+    SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=... PAYFAST_PASSPHRASE=... RESEND_API_KEY=... \
+    THE_COURIER_GUY_API_KEY=... SHIPPING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=... \
+    node scripts/staging/scan-deployed-bundles.mjs https://<customer>.onrender.com https://<admin>.onrender.com
+
+A value check that was not exported is reported as SKIPPED, never as passed.
+Also check in Render > each service > Environment: every server-only secret exists as a
+plain variable with NO `VITE_` prefix, and there is no `VITE_` twin of any of them.
+
+## 5. Sandbox checkout  (blocker 3)
+See the notes in the pull request: the current code does not redirect to PayFast, so this
+step needs the checkout change before it can pass.
